# Line endings. The test suite and the Render deploy both run on Linux, and a
# CRLF checkout fails a dozen tests (anything that compares a file's bytes or
# splits a template on "\n"). The owner's Windows machine has the system-level
# core.autocrlf=true, so until this file existed the only thing keeping
# checkouts LF was an unversioned .git/config entry -- and ten files still
# landed in the index as CRLF. This normalizes every text file to LF in the
# repo AND in the working tree, on every clone, whatever the local config says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary

# Generated, minified, one line: a diff of it is noise.
tailwind.css -diff
